   "why_it_matters": "`preauth_at` is the owner window's opening time and the only lower bound on the signing order. Without a zone the predicate `preauth_at < verify_pass_at <= signed_at` is evaluated in whatever zone the reader assumes; read as UTC it is 08:00 later than read as +08:00, so a bundle that would fail the order check under one reading passes under the other",
   "not_fixed_here": "the bundle and the signed envelope are signatures; rewriting either would change a signed payload digest and produce a receipt that no owner signed. This round does not re-sign",
   "closes_when": "the owner re-signs a semantic acceptance whose body carries `preauthorised_at` WITH an explicit offset (the body already does: sign_r26.py writes `win['opened_at']` into `body.preauthorised_at`) and republishes a bundle whose `sequence.preauth_at` is the same qualified string; then payload_sha256 and signature_hex change and this verifier must be re-run against the new envelope",
   "exact_resign_scope": {
    "envelope": "receipts/OWNER_SEMANTIC_ACK_R26.signed.json (new file, new payload_sha256)",
    "bundle_fields": [
     "sequence.preauth_at",
     "sequence.verify_pass_at",
     "sequence.signed_at",
     "semantic_ack.payload_sha256",
     "semantic_ack.signature_hex_prefix"
    ],
    "documented_by": "the new bundle must state the offset it qualifies all three with"
   }
